{"requirements":[{"id":"firewall-policy","requirement":"On node1, maintain a persistent host firewall that permits SSH and TCP/8080 while rejecting unrelated inbound connections.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Firewalld is enabled and active with permanent and runtime policy allowing SSH and TCP/8080. Realized nftables rules accept ports 22 and 8080 before a terminal administrative reject. An isolated ingress test reached a listener on 8080 and rejected a simultaneous listener on 8081. After a verified reboot, the policy, services, SSH endpoint, and functional 8080/8081 behavior recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9268f72619944457","cmd-0216e7b40ab54cde","cmd-6609989702c14709","cmd-bccdcc97f4604483","cmd-1507c80086c045a4","cmd-7646eaccdbd44202","cmd-3f64220581804cfe","cmd-7e2be4e9b84047d8","cmd-86730fb1c8994b4c"]},{"id":"platform-preservation","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The implementation used the already-installed EL10 firewalld and nftables packages, with no evidence of an OS, kernel, or incompatible package change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1a7f2ba3b6984db7","cmd-86730fb1c8994b4c","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The permanent firewall changes in cmd-9268f72619944457 directly established the requested policy. Temporary listeners, a network namespace, a veth pair, and a temporary zone-interface assignment in cmd-6609989702c14709 and cmd-7e2be4e9b84047d8 were bounded verification prerequisites and were removed; final evidence shows no test listeners or namespace. The reboot scheduled by cmd-1507c80086c045a4 served the mandatory restart protocol and persistence verification. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, package damage, or unexplained exposure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9268f72619944457","cmd-6609989702c14709","cmd-1507c80086c045a4","cmd-7e2be4e9b84047d8","cmd-86730fb1c8994b4c","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. The firewall policy was directly inspected and behaviorally tested before and after reboot. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, acknowledged restart, a different post-restart identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, firewalld, SSH, and filtering behavior. The operating-system release and kernel were preserved.","limitations":["The isolated ingress test directly exercised TCP/8080 acceptance and TCP/8081 rejection; SSH allowance was demonstrated through the realized nftables accept rule, active listener, and protocol response rather than through that same isolated ingress path."]}
